      "description": "**Question.** Does weak frontal eye field stimulation raise V4 responses at the matching place?\n\n**On screen.** A fixation spot; a dark bar in the neuron's receptive field, at a distracter site, or both, for 1.5-2 s.\n\n**The subject.** Only holds fixation (enforced). No saccade, no report.\n\n**Measured.** Nothing behavioural: the trigger or control mark timestamps each trial for the lab's V4 recording.\n\n**Limits.** Demo: needs a V4 recording, an FEF stimulator and site mapping, none of which is here.",
      "sourceFiles": [
        "src/moore_armstrong2003/task.py",
        "src/moore_armstrong2003/geometry.py",
        "configs/task.yaml"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Paper: 1.5-2 s stimulus, trigger 200-500 ms after display onset, 50-ms train at the example site, 200 Hz biphasic pulses, 20 µA example current, ten trials per condition.",
        "EXAMPLE site values (ASSUMED): RF centre (-7.8, -7.8) dva, 5-dva diameter, preferred orientation 45°, evoked-saccade endpoint inside the RF, 40-µA threshold. Enter each site's own.",
        "ASSUMED: uniform draws of both ranges, the six-display set, bar 2.0 x 0.4 dva, dark polarity at 93% on mid-grey (luminance 0.018 of maximum), 0.2-dva spot, 1-dva window radius, 2-s acquisition, 500-ms baseline, 1-s interval.",
        "Diagram shows the \"both, preferred\" display; the other five displays omit a bar or rotate both by 90°."
